    "title": "Concept: Direct Proportion",
    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Direct proportion describes a special relationship between two variables where one increases at a constant rate as the other increases. This relationship can be written as <em>y = kx</em> or <em>y &propto; x</em>, where <strong>k</strong> is the constant of proportionality. The graph will always be a straight line passing through the origin (0,0).</p>",
