    "explanation": "<p class=\"text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground\">Inverse proportion is a relationship where one variable increases as the other decreases at a reciprocal rate. It is written as <em>y = k/x</em> or <em>y &propto; 1/x</em>. The graph produced is a reciprocal curve (hyperbola) that approaches both axes but never touches them.</p>",
